jess: Streaming responses from the Node TS SDK keep hanging mid-stream after our auth token rotates and the SDK does an automatic retry. Repro on Vercel Edge (edge runtime). Started after upgrading redwood-node@2.4.0 -> 2.4.1. Anyone seen this?

support-bot: Thanks @jess — acknowledged. Can you paste a minimal repro and a request_id from a failing run?

jess: Repro steps (short):
1) run on Vercel Edge (edge runtime) + node 18 compat
2) start a streaming generation using the SDK's streaming helper
3) trigger token rotation (short-lived token refresh), cause first request to get 401, SDK retries automatically
4) first attempt returns chunks, retry succeeds, but after the retry the ReadableStream hangs (no more chunks, reader.read() never resolves)

Code snippet (TS):
```ts
const res = await client.stream({ model: 'gpt-open:edge-opt', input: prompt });
const reader = res.body?.getReader();
const decoder = new TextDecoder();
while (true) {
  const { done, value } = await reader!.read();
  if (done) break;
  console.log(decoder.decode(value));
}
```

jess: Logs from the session: (sensitive parts removed)
```
[2026-03-15T18:22:31Z] req=req_01Habc123 status=401 auth=expired token_ts=161823
[2026-03-15T18:22:31Z] req=req_01Habc123 retry=1 status=200 stream_open
[2026-03-15T18:22:32Z] req=req_01Habc123 chunk=...
[2026-03-15T18:22:33Z] req=req_01Habc123 stream_stall read_timeout=30000
```

elena: Thanks — can you also paste the exact SDK version and the request_id (looks like req_01Habc123 above). Is this reproducible without Vercel (e.g., local node or Cloudflare)?

jess: SDK version: "@redwood/inference-node" 2.4.1. Confirmed repro locally using the edge shim (node fetch polyfills) but behavior is most obvious on Vercel Edge. Request id: req_01Habc123. Repro link (private gist with minimal app): https://gist.example.com/priv/repro-187234 (token removed)

marco: This rings a bell — in edge runtimes the ReadableStream reader can get into a locked/abandoned state if the underlying response object is reused during retries. If the SDK retries by creating a new fetch but reuses internal stream objects, the original reader might be left waiting.

marco: Quick narrow ideas: 1) try disabling SDK automatic retries (set retry: 0) and implement a manual retry wrapper that tears down the reader before retrying; 2) pin back to 2.4.0 where you said it worked; 3) as a short-term workaround use a raw fetch against the inference endpoint and pipe the body manually.

jess: Tried retry:0 — streaming works (no hang). Pinning to 2.4.0 also fixes it. So looks like the regression is in 2.4.1 retry path.

devex: Can you paste the SDK config you used? e.g. token refresh hook or middleware? The interaction with tokenRotation handlers can matter.

jess: We use an auth refresh handler that swaps the Authorization header mid-flight — code roughly:
```ts
client.setAuthProvider(async () => {
  if (tokenExpired) {
    await rotateToken();
  }
  return `Bearer ${currentToken}`;
});
```
There is a small window where first request gets 401, handler rotates token, SDK retries.

elena: Thanks — that helps. Can you confirm the response headers for the successful retry include Transfer-Encoding: chunked (they should) and that Content-Length is not present? If the server returns Content-Length (or Vercel edge buffers) the stream might be treated as non-chunked.

jess: Server returns chunked on the retry. I attached a netlog snippet in the gist.

marco: For the eng-runtime team: suspicious area is sdk/streaming -> retry codepath that re-attaches a new Response body to an existing ReadableStream controller without releasing the old reader lock. Workaround for customers: pin to 2.4.0 or set retry:0. We'll need a hotfix to ensure reader locks are cleared on retry.

elena: I've escalated this to #eng-runtime, tagging @runtime-team. Marking P2 since it affects streaming apps on edge.

oncall-bot: Incident created: INC-2026-03-187 (streaming-hang-after-retry). Assigned to eng-runtime.

elena: Action items for support: please collect 1) minimal repro, 2) request ids (we have req_01Habc123), 3) SDK debug logs with DEBUG=redwood:streaming enabled, and 4) server response headers for the retry. jess — can you upload the debug logs to the gist?

jess: Uploaded debug logs to the gist and added notes about how to reproduce on local with the edge shim. Thanks — temporary fix will be pin to 2.4.0 in prod.

elena: Great — devs will triage the fix. We'll follow up here with a patch/PR link. :thumbsup:
